# Pinned third-party downloads for the server (Lightsail, and the Mac
# mini's container). Sourced by provision.sh; plain KEY=VALUE, no commands.
# Every download is verified against the SHA-256 below before it is used,
# and provisioning stops on a mismatch. Change a pin only deliberately, and
# say in the pull request where the new value came from
# (docs/runbooks/lightsail-deployment.md, "Bumping a pinned version").

# IBC (IbcAlpha/IBC), the Gateway login controller.
# Source: https://github.com/IbcAlpha/IBC/releases/tag/3.24.2 (GitHub releases
# API, published 2026-08-21). The release publishes no checksum; the value
# below is the SHA-256 of the IBCLinux-3.24.2.zip asset as downloaded on
# 2026-10-16.
IBC_VERSION=3.24.2
IBC_URL=https://github.com/IbcAlpha/IBC/releases/download/3.24.2/IBCLinux-3.24.2.zip
IBC_SHA256=cc097ca1dfa75413a5fbe02e4743050af15f3308eb6a97c769b3cff9850c80c5

# IB Gateway, stable standalone installer for Linux x64.
# Source: Interactive Brokers, https://www.interactivebrokers.com/en/trading/ibgateway-stable.php
# The installer URL is IBKR's moving "stable" link and the version is read from
# https://download2.interactivebrokers.com/installers/ibgateway/stable-standalone/version.json
# (buildVersion 10.50.1f, 2026-10-05). IBKR publishes no checksum; the SHA-256
# below is of the file downloaded on 2026-10-16. When IBKR replaces the file
# the checksum no longer matches and `provision.sh gateway` (and `all`) stops,
# which is intended: ADR 0025 point 5 requires the paper-account coverage test
# to be repeated on a Gateway version change before the pin moves.
GATEWAY_BUILD=10.50.1f
GATEWAY_MAJOR=1050
GATEWAY_URL=https://download2.interactivebrokers.com/installers/ibgateway/stable-standalone/ibgateway-stable-standalone-linux-x64.sh
GATEWAY_SHA256=2b868362238cef71ee0f83068c6e5777ae38f59eae585ff84f75ca1d8b2e06d5

# IBKR's TWS API, whose Python client (ibapi) the IBKR adapter uses (ADR 0025
# point 4, amended 2026-10-16: fetched and verified, never committed).
# Source: Interactive Brokers, https://download2.interactivebrokers.com/installers/tws-api/index.html
# IBKR's page says only the "Latest" Mac/Linux build includes the Python API
# (v1051.01 on 2026-10-18; "Stable", v1050.02, has Java and C++ only), so the
# pin is Latest. The URL is IBKR's moving "latest" link and IBKR publishes no
# checksum; the SHA-256 below is of the file downloaded on 2026-10-18
# (61,566,272 bytes, Last-Modified 2026-10-02). When IBKR replaces the file
# the checksum no longer matches and `provision.sh twsapi` stops (its own
# step, outside `all`, so the Gateway and services still provision), which is intended:
# ADR 0025 point 5 requires the paper-account coverage test to be repeated on
# an API version change before the pin moves.
TWSAPI_VERSION=10.51.01
TWSAPI_URL=https://download2.interactivebrokers.com/installers/tws-api/latest/tws-api-latest-linux-x64.sh
TWSAPI_SHA256=152af944be28bcfaf2733aec907e7724f6dda092cb3148848e84d2a0bb866c0a
# The same release's Mac/Unix archive, which `provision.sh twsapi` installs
# from on arm64 (the Mac mini's container), where the x86_64-only installer
# above cannot run: it starts its own bundled x86_64 Java and accepts no other
# (owner decision 2026-10-18: pin this archive, no emulation). A plain zip;
# only its IBJts/source/pythonclient is used. Source: Interactive Brokers'
# own site, interactivebrokers.github.io/downloads/ (the versioned file name
# IBKR has always used for this archive; today's download page links the
# installers only). Its IBJts/API_VersionNum.txt says API_Version=10.51.01,
# the version above. IBKR publishes no checksum; the SHA-256 below is of the
# file downloaded on 2026-10-18 (11,412,901 bytes, Last-Modified
# 2026-10-09). The record the step writes names this SHA-256 with
# TWSAPI_ARTEFACT=archive on arm64; the adapter accepts the installer's record
# only on x86_64 and the archive's only on arm64 (adapter/ibkr/ibapi_pin.py). Both pins move together.
TWSAPI_ARCHIVE_URL=https://interactivebrokers.github.io/downloads/twsapi_macunix.1051.01.zip
TWSAPI_ARCHIVE_SHA256=50a459ed09f0030df25125a177e57b69bdf576ec3a89fcb1f81fdff95bbf6316

# protobuf, the Python package ibapi imports as google.protobuf (10.51.01
# needs 5.29.5; Ubuntu 24.04's packaged 3.21.12 does not work). A new runtime
# dependency under docs/dependency-policy.md, proposed to the owner 2026-10-20.
# Source: PyPI, https://pypi.org/project/protobuf/5.29.5/ (BSD-3-Clause,
# uploaded 2025-05-28). The pure-Python wheel, one file for amd64 and arm64
# alike; its SHA-256 is the digest PyPI's JSON API
# (https://pypi.org/pypi/protobuf/5.29.5/json) lists for that file, checked
# against the downloaded file on 2026-10-20. `provision.sh twsapi` installs it
# offline into the adapter's environment before ibapi.
PROTOBUF_VERSION=5.29.5
PROTOBUF_URL=https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/7e/cc/7e77861000a0691aeea8f4566e5d3aa716f2b1dece4a24439437e41d3d25/protobuf-5.29.5-py3-none-any.whl
PROTOBUF_SHA256=6cf42630262c59b2d8de33954443d94b746c952b01434fc58a417fdbd2e84bd5

# Tailscale static binaries (linux amd64).
# Source: https://pkgs.tailscale.com/stable/ ; the checksum is the contents of
# https://pkgs.tailscale.com/stable/tailscale_1.104.1_amd64.tgz.sha256
TAILSCALE_VERSION=1.104.1
TAILSCALE_URL=https://pkgs.tailscale.com/stable/tailscale_1.104.1_amd64.tgz
TAILSCALE_SHA256=108d1d96ecf410d305571e173516f27038f870919a9b89c914a167c6d33a4528

# ntfy server (binwiederhier/ntfy), the owner's own push server, which takes
# the daily summary and never leaves the Tailscale address (docs/manual/server.md,
# "Your own ntfy server"). The summary carries balances, so it never goes to
# the public ntfy.sh relay or to PagerDuty.
# Source: https://github.com/binwiederhier/ntfy/releases/tag/v2.29.0 (published
# 2026-10-07; the newest release at least two weeks old when pinned). The SHA-256
# is the line for ntfy_2.29.0_linux_amd64.tar.gz in the release's checksums.txt,
# and equals the SHA-256 of the file downloaded on 2026-10-21.
NTFY_VERSION=2.29.0
NTFY_URL=https://github.com/binwiederhier/ntfy/releases/download/v2.29.0/ntfy_2.29.0_linux_amd64.tar.gz
NTFY_SHA256=7862bcb9bc422d9f442fffa72b6393386475f880079edd0978a5d31d3307314e
